# checklist.md
# Migration checklist: pg

- [ ] Choose microservice import for one database (roles are not imported) or monolith import for several databases (roles lose SUPERUSER; postgres is skipped). ([source](https://cloudnative-pg.io/docs/1.30/database_import))
- [ ] Stop writes on the source before the final import; later changes are not copied. ([source](https://cloudnative-pg.io/docs/1.30/database_import))
- [ ] Use a destination PostgreSQL major at least as new as the source; destination pg_dump is used. ([source](https://cloudnative-pg.io/docs/1.30/database_import))
- [ ] Size PGDATA for the staged dump, data, and indexes. ([source](https://cloudnative-pg.io/docs/1.30/database_import))
- [ ] Ensure the source is reachable and the import user can run pg_dump and read roles. ([source](https://cloudnative-pg.io/docs/1.30/database_import))
- [ ] CloudNativePG defaults ssl_min_protocol_version to TLSv1.3; verify whether clients need TLS 1.2. ([source](https://cloudnative-pg.io/docs/1.30/postgresql_conf))

